course: dictionary
lesson: 5772
title: Finding meaning from clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Break a new word into parts you already know. Lungfish is made of lung and fish. A lung is the part of your body that breathes air, so a lungfish is a fish that can breathe air as well as use gills.
explain: Read the words around the word for more clues. «In dried-up pools a lungfish sleeps in a ball of mud until the rain comes back.» The mud and the waiting for rain tell you the fish can survive when its pond dries up.
explain: Check your guess by putting your meaning into the sentence. «The shoebill stands still for hours, waiting for lungfish to come up to breathe.» A fish that can breathe air fits this, because it comes up to the top to breathe.
fact: Lungfish are freshwater fish, so they live in fresh water, not the sea.
fact: Lungfish can breathe with gills like other fish, and they can also breathe air with lungs.
fact: Some lungfish bury themselves in mud when their pond dries up, and they can breathe air for months.
fact: «Aestivation» is a long summer sleep, and «African lungfish» are one animal that does it.
fact: «Lungfish» is a noun, and the plural can be lungfish or lungfishes.
exercise: «In dried-up pools a lungfish sleeps in a ball of mud until the rain comes back.» Where does the lungfish sleep? | In a tall tree | In the sea | *In a ball of mud | On the rocks by the river
exercise: Jade thinks lungfish must be a fish with a big mouth. What does lungfish mean? | *A freshwater fish that can breathe air with lungs as well as gills | A bird with a long beak | A fish with no fins at all | A fish that lives only in the sea
exercise: «Some animals sleep through summer instead.» What is that summer sleep called? | A loud clattering noise | A type of rain | *Aestivation | A fishing net
test: What does «survive» mean in «Some lungfish can survive when their pond dries up»? | To dry up | *To stay alive through hard times | To stay alive | To swim very fast
test: A lungfish has gills and lungs. What are its lungs used for? | To lay eggs | To hear sounds | *To breathe air | To swim faster
exam: What does the shoebill wait for, in «The shoebill stands still for hours waiting for lungfish to come up to breathe»? | A storm to pass | A boat to pass by | The rain to stop | *Lungfish to come up to breathe
